\section*{Hodge classes on powers of split Weil sixfolds}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Algebraicity is claimed for Hodge classes on powers of split Weil sixfolds and of abelian varieties of dimension at most five carrying an imaginary-quadratic action, including special periods. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 032, 2026-09-30): A coherent seed and its Fourier--Mukai transform produce the split-sixfold Weil plane through an obstruction calculation and deformation. A determinant description of the actual Hodge group, combined with the CM result, extends these algebraic generators to powers and to the stated low-dimensional cases.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
